{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_58405bfc-5284-504d-bb32-dbae6e09cdbf",
  "name": "3.1 Angle types, complements and supplements",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Angle types, complements and supplements"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Classify angles and calculate complementary and supplementary pairs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An acute angle lies between 0° and 90°; a right angle is 90°; an obtuse angle is between 90° and 180°; a straight angle is 180°; a reflex angle is greater than 180° and less than 360°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Complementary angles add to 90°. Supplementary angles add to 180°. They do not have to be adjacent. Subtract the given angle from the appropriate total to find its complement or supplement."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockImage",
        "attrs": {
          "blockObject": {
            "block_uuid": "block_dc369eae-4e44-5b70-974e-a6e587672cf8",
            "content": {
              "file_id": "81e82abf-5649-516b-b3d0-ac1e8e9da0d8",
              "file_format": "png",
              "activity_uuid": "activity_58405bfc-5284-504d-bb32-dbae6e09cdbf"
            }
          },
          "size": {
            "width": 900
          },
          "alignment": "center",
          "unsplash_url": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_name": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_url": null,
          "unsplash_photo_url": null
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Compare the measured openings; the labelled reflex arc extends beyond a straight angle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Find the complement of 37°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "90° − 37° = 53°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Find the supplement of 126°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "180° − 126° = 54°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Independent practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work these out in your notebook before looking at the self-check below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
